[{:db/id -1, :docs.pilot-2-design/body "# 2nd Outbound Pilot Design — 100 Sites / 4 Weeks\n\n**Version**: iter-57 (2026-05-28)\n**Status**: Design (ready to launch once deploy/verify 1-tile passes)\n**Parent ADR**: [ADR-2605281130 §iter-46+ runbook](../../../90-docs/adr/2605281130-jp-ashiba-q2-strategy-satellite-evo-x2-mailer-langgraph.md)\n**Test oracle (1-tile)**: `00-contracts/datomic/jp-ashiba/fixtures/expected-1tile-datoms.edn`\n\n## Why a second pilot\n\niter-43 audit demoted 10 hypotheses tied to the first pilot — most importantly\n`cs_q2_outbound_japan_8`, `r_outbound_cac_payback`, `km_outbound_conv_8`,\n`p_q2_invisible_demand`. The first pilot's 5/6–5/7 burst (40 emails, CF Analytics\nconfirmed) proved the pipeline works once, but a 20-day dormancy meant we have no\nmeasured conversion. This pilot replaces those `false` claims with measured truth.\n\n## Hypotheses being tested (validation targets)\n\n| Hypothesis | Threshold to validate | Current state |\n|---|---|---|\n| `p_q2_invisible_demand` | ≥ 25-day lead-time reduction observed in ≥ 5 wins | `false` (iter-43 demote) |\n| `cs_q2_outbound_japan_8` | ≥ 6 contracted customers in pilot window | `false` |\n| `ch_q2_outbound_pilot` | conv ≥ 6% on 100-site sample | `false` |\n| `km_outbound_conv_8` | conv ≥ 8% sustained for 14 consecutive days | `false` |\n| `r_outbound_cac_payback` | CAC ≤ ¥45K/social, payback ≤ 1.5 months | `false` |\n| `ua_did_30000` | DID ≥ 30K post-pilot | `false` |\n\n## Sample selection\n\n- **N = 100 construction sites** detected by `satellite_detector` on Sentinel-2 imagery 2026-05-15 → 2026-05-29\n- **Geographic spread**: Tokyo 23-ku 40, Kanagawa 20, Saitama 20, Chiba 20 (matches existing scaffold-supplier coverage)\n- **Confidence filter**: `:ashiba/confidence >= 0.75` (oracle threshold; 1-tile sample shows 0.85)\n- **Match filter**: `:ashiba/match-rate >= 0.75` (owner-resolver hit)\n- **Stratification**: residential 60 / commercial 30 / public 10 (per JIS A 8951 demand distribution)\n\n## Timeline\n\n```\nWeek 1: deploy + 1-tile smoke (gate)\n  - Day 1   : preflight 9/9 + smoke + docker buildx + kubectl apply\n  - Day 2   : zbctl deploy + kotoba schema seed\n  - Day 3   : 1-tile smoke (verify_1tile.sh 6/6)\n  - Day 4–5 : run 5 additional verification tiles across 5 prefectures\n\nWeek 2: satellite detection batch\n  - Day 8–10: 100-tile Sentinel-2 batch run\n              kotoba q `(:find ?sid :where [?sid :ashiba/confidence ?c] [(>= ?c 0.75)])`\n              must return ≥ 100 site_ids\n\nWeek 3: outbound send + reply window\n  - Day 11–12: owner-resolver + outbound-emailer batch on the 100 sites\n               mailer.gftd.ai sendEmail × N (rate-limited 25/hour to stay under Resend free-tier)\n  - Day 13–24: monitor inbound replies via vertex_mailer_inbound_email\n               kotoba q for replies tagged X-Ashiba-Site-Id\n\nWeek 4: measurement + decision\n  - Day 25–28: tally conversions, CAC, payback, lead-time reduction\n               kotoba q against the run_graph + vertex_mailer_inbound_email\n               write iter-58 BMC with measured values (replacing `false` with `true|false`)\n```\n\n## Measurement plan (kotoba queries)\n\nAll four metrics computed from the same `run_graph = kotoba://graph/ashiba:run:pilot-2`.\n\n```clojure\n;; M1: conversion rate (# replied 'interested' / # sent)\n[:find (count ?sid)\n :where [?sid :ashiba/mailer-message-id ?mid]\n        [?mid :mailer/reply-classification :interested]]\n;; ÷\n[:find (count ?sid)\n :where [?sid :ashiba/mailer-message-id ?mid]\n        [(not= ?mid \"failed\")]]\n\n;; M2: contracted count (# moved to kakin.gftd.ai)\n[:find (count ?sid)\n :where [?sid :ashiba/mailer-message-id ?mid]\n        [?mid :kakin/contract-id ?_]]\n\n;; M3: lead-time reduction (median between Sentinel-2 epoch and reply date)\n[:find (avg ?delta-days)\n :where [?sid :ashiba/epoch ?epoch]\n        [?sid :ashiba/mailer-message-id ?mid]\n        [?mid :mailer/replied-at ?replied]\n        [(date-diff ?epoch ?replied) ?delta-days]]\n\n;; M4: CAC (Planet Labs cost + ETL + Murakumo tokens) / contracted count\n;; (computed off-graph from invoices since cost is monthly fixed)\n```\n\n## Decision criteria\n\nAfter Week 4 measurement, decide one of three:\n\n### KILL\nAny of:\n- conv < 2% (sample too cold for outbound)\n- CAC > ¥70K (worse than original cloud-GPU baseline; Datomic + EVO-X2 didn't help)\n- 0 contracted (proposal-vendor matching failed)\n\nThen: revert `sol_satellite_pipeline_ga` future hypothesis, archive 4-actor pipeline,\nfocus Q3 on inbound (SEO + Jasindo) only.\n\n### PIVOT\nAny of:\n- conv 2–6% (lukewarm, prompt-engineering pivot needed)\n- conv 6%+ but contracted = 0 (lead quality bad — owner-resolver match accuracy or vendor matching)\n\nThen: rebuild Murakumo prompt + run another 100-site pilot at iter-65. Update BMC with\n`pivot` validation state.\n\n### SCALE\nAll of:\n- conv ≥ 6% sustained\n- ≥ 6 contracted customers\n- CAC ≤ ¥45K, payback ≤ 1.5 months\n\nThen: update all 6 demoted hypotheses to `validated=true`. Scale to 500/month (Q2 末 target).\nMaturity moves to 5/5 in `customer_segments`, `revenue`, `channels`, `key_metrics`. BMC → 5.0 ★★★★★.\n\n## Operational discipline\n\n1. **Daily kotoba q() snapshot** at 09:00 JST — write to `_working/pilot-2/{YYYY-MM-DD}.json`\n2. **Mailer drift alert** stays armed (coverage.dl `mailer_drift_alert :- gap > 20`) — pages if claim ≠ measured\n3. **CACAO-signed daily summary** — `kotoba sparql --cacao` against the run_graph, signed by `did:web:gftdcojp.gftd.ai`\n4. **No claims in BMC without a measured kotoba q() row** — strict from iter-43 audit forward\n\n## Rollback during pilot\n\nIf verify_1tile.sh fails mid-pilot:\n```bash\nkubectl -n jp-ashiba-langgraph rollout undo deploy/jp-ashiba-langgraph\n# pilot data in run_graph kotoba://graph/ashiba:run:pilot-2 is preserved (immutable)\n# decide whether to continue with previous image or abort entire pilot\n```\n\n## What is NOT in this pilot\n\n- ASEAN/Indonesia tiles (Q2 末)\n- v7 safety-predictor integration (separate parallel pilot iter-60+)\n- Jasindo loss-control feedback loop (Q2 末)\n- Planet Labs SkySat (Sentinel-2 only; Planet is for Q2 末 GA)\n\n## References\n\n- [RUNBOOK-deploy.md](./RUNBOOK-deploy.md) — operator playbook (iter-55)\n- [ADR-2605281130](../../../90-docs/adr/2605281130-jp-ashiba-q2-strategy-satellite-evo-x2-mailer-langgraph.md) — Q2 strategy\n- 1-tile fixtures: `00-contracts/datomic/jp-ashiba/fixtures/`\n- Measurement helpers: `coverage.dl` (Datalog rules for mailer drift / conversion)\n"}]